domain ConsciousRequiredFieldsRca:
  description "Read-only RCA of missing fields in the latest production battle"

problem REQUIRED_FIELDS:
  |
    Explain why normal-turn conscious decisions omit required fields, distinguish
    confirmed contract wiring defects from model-behavior hypotheses, and identify
    a repair direction that preserves producer-owned goal, intent and speech.
    Scope is analysis only: no gameplay implementation, migration, provider call,
    production write, or deployment is performed by this investigation.

evidence LIVE_PATTERN:
  |
    Latest battle btl_e24ccddf1d8ec96b0073323f2bf256db finished at
    2026-10-03 06:34:50 JST in 18 turns. Saved primary normal-turn traces cover
    turns 1..17, both sides: 34 outputs. Eleven B outputs, turns
    2,4,6,7,8,9,11,13,14,15,16, have the same missing fields: initialGoal,
    nextUtterance, realizedManifestation. intent and nextAction decode validly.
    Input phase and decoded phase are turn, and the existing upper goal is present.
    Source: docs/evidence/conscious-required-fields-replay-2026-10-03.json.
    Raw HTTP response bytes and exact deployed request bodies were not retained
    in this artifact; decoded missing markers do not prove model internal intent.

evidence REQUEST_WIRING:
  |
    backend/src/llm/conscious-agency.ts consciousRequest explicitly preserves
    input.phase, agencyState and decision. openai-compatible.ts
    advanceCharacterAgent contractVersion=3 calls consciousRequest, chatJson,
    then consciousResult(raw,input.phase). The current-source path does not
    intentionally rename turn to later or remove response fields before decoding.
    This is source evidence, not a packet capture of each historical request.

evidence MIXED_PHASE_PROMPT:
  |
    CONSCIOUS_V3_PROMPT contains all phase rules in one system instruction:
    prologue/turn needs five fields; aftermath needs two expression fields;
    later needs only intent and nextAction. Every normal V3 request receives
    the later rule as well. The eleven observed two-field shapes match the later
    grammar. CHARACTER_ACTION_PROPOSAL_OUTPUT_RULES adds nested action shapes;
    it does not require removal of the other top-level conscious fields.

evidence JSON_ONLY_BOUNDARY:
  |
    openai-compatible.ts advanceCharacterAgentCompact does not set responseFormat.
    chatJson therefore sends response_format={type:json_object}, rather than
    a phase-specific strict JSON schema with required field names. JSON validity
    alone does not enforce the conscious five-field contract. Other operations
    in the same adapter already support responseFormat and validate xAI schemas.

evidence DECODER_AND_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    packages/shared/src/conscious-agency.ts field uses Object.hasOwn: an omitted
    key is missing, distinct from an explicit null. decodeConsciousOutputV3
    checks allowed keys but preserves individual missing field markers.
    acceptConsciousDecisionV3 requires initialGoal.valid before accepting a turn
    decision even when the goal already exists; existing goals require explicit
    null and cannot be replaced. Speech and manifestation are decoded separately.
    A valid JSON response can therefore be an invalid application decision.

evidence NO_APPLICATION_REPAIR:
  |
    chatJson parses JSON and records provider-call success. Provider HTTP retry
    is distinct from domain repair. The normal V3 caller immediately returns
    consciousResult and has no bounded missing-field regeneration loop.
    Decoder-produced missing markers do not throw a transport exception.
    battle-service.ts converts agency non-acceptance into schema_invalid and
    accepts expression independently. Therefore HTTP success is not decision
    acceptance and field failure does not automatically trigger another model.

evidence COUNTERFACTUAL_REPLAY:
  |
    Offline replay of each missing-field trace reproduces goal_invalid. Changing
    only a copied decoded initialGoal field to valid explicit null accepts
    10 of the 11 decisions under the saved action-validation outcomes; turn 2
    remains action_invalid due to unavailable_instrument. This isolates the
    immediate acceptance gate; it is not evidence that omitted speech meant
    silence, nor permission to normalize production omissions to null.
    All 10 newly accepted decisions are wait. Field completion alone consequently
    does not demonstrate varied tactics or solve match monotony.

decision CONFIRMED_CAUSAL_CHAIN based_on REQUIRED_FIELDS, LIVE_PATTERN, JSON_ONLY_BOUNDARY, DECODER_AND_ACCEPTANCE, NO_APPLICATION_REPAIR, COUNTERFACTUAL_REPLAY:
  |
    Confirmed chain: an external JSON object lacks three phase-required keys;
    the boundary accepts JSON without enforcing the phase grammar; the decoder
    exposes missing initialGoal; agency acceptance rejects the whole intent/action
    pair; no domain repair obtains a complete output and the rejection reason is
    collapsed. Ten saved otherwise-valid wait proposals are blocked at this gate.
    This is a producer-boundary and recovery gap, not a TypeScript union failure.

decision PHASE_CONFUSION_HYPOTHESIS based_on LIVE_PATTERN, REQUEST_WIRING, MIXED_PHASE_PROMPT:
  |
    The strongest working hypothesis is output-phase confusion caused or enabled
    by shared instructions containing incompatible phase envelopes. The repeated
    exact later shape supports this more than isolated random key loss. However,
    absent raw request/response capture and a controlled phase-prompt comparison,
    the model's reason cannot be asserted as proven. Existing-goal omission or
    suppression of all nullable fields is an alternative consistent with the data.

decision REPAIR_CANDIDATE based_on CONFIRMED_CAUSAL_CHAIN, PHASE_CONFUSION_HYPOTHESIS:
  |
    Candidate direction, not an accepted architectural change: build only the
    active phase instruction and enforce its required-key grammar through the
    provider's supported strict schema. Keep reference grounding, current action
    availability, immutable-goal ownership and partial expression acceptance in
    domain validation. Preserve exact field-level and agency failure reasons.
    If domain repair is adopted, specify a bounded same-context re-generation
    contract with accounting, failure handling and independent speech ownership.
    Never invent goal, intent, action or speech, fill missing values merely to
    pass types, or treat absence as the producer's explicit choice of silence.

decision VERIFICATION_BOUNDARY based_on REPAIR_CANDIDATE, COUNTERFACTUAL_REPLAY, MIXED_PHASE_PROMPT:
  |
    Next verification should test active-phase instructions and outgoing strict
    schemas for turn/later/aftermath, missing versus explicit null, fixed upper
    goals, current reference/action validity, independently accepted speech, and
    useful failure feedback. Any live comparison must measure missing-field rate,
    decision acceptance, action distribution, repeated utterances, usage and latency;
    field-complete repeated waits are not quality acceptance. New retry or public
    contract choices need their governing ADR before implementation. This analysis
    does not create or execute such a policy and does not replay the live battle.
